From: OpenWrt <openwrt@openwrt.org>
Subject: realtek: rtl83xx: l3: avoid collision with 7.3 at_least macro

Linux 7.3 defines at_least as a macro in include/linux/compiler_types.h
(expands to "static" unless __CHECKER__). The realtek DSA driver's
otto_l3_prefix_rows() uses at_least as a parameter name and in its body, so
the macro expansion breaks both the declaration and the comparison:

  drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c:1608:39: error: 'static' is not at beginning of declaration
  drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c:1608:39: error: storage class specified for unnamed parameter
  drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c:1615:62: error: expected expression before 'static'

Rename the parameter to min_prefix_len. All callers pass it positionally,
so only these two sites need changing.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@openwrt.org>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c
@@ -1605,14 +1605,14 @@
  * matching row rather than the most specific one. A lookup carries the entry
  * type, so a block is only ever matched against its own family.
  */
-static int otto_l3_prefix_rows(struct otto_l3_ctrl *ctrl, u8 type, int at_least)
+static int otto_l3_prefix_rows(struct otto_l3_ctrl *ctrl, u8 type, int min_prefix_len)
 {
 	struct otto_l3_route *q;
 	int n = 0;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(q, &ctrl->routes_list, list) {
 		if (!q->is_host_route && q->row >= 0 &&
-		    q->attr.type == type && q->prefix_len >= at_least)
+		    q->attr.type == type && q->prefix_len >= min_prefix_len)
 			n++;
 	}
 
